## Configuration Details

| Component | Configuration |
|---|---|
| Number of instances | 3 |
| Instance type | t2.micro |
| Key pair | devops-key |
| AMI | Latest Amazon Linux 2 |
| Resource type | aws_instance |
| Terraform meta-argument | count |
| AWS region | us-east-1 |
| Resource naming prefix | devops-instance |

## 1. Main Terraform Configuration

**File: `main.tf`**

```hcl
resource "aws_instance" "kke_instance" {
  count         = var.KKE_INSTANCE_COUNT
  ami           = local.AMI_ID
  instance_type = var.KKE_INSTANCE_TYPE
  key_name      = var.KKE_KEY_NAME

  tags = {
    Name = "${var.KKE_INSTANCE_PREFIX}-${count.index + 1}"
  }
}
```

This resource uses `count` to create three instances from one resource definition. The `count.index` expression generates unique instance names.

## 2. Input Variables

**File: `variables.tf`**

```hcl
variable "KKE_INSTANCE_COUNT" {
  type        = number
  description = "Number of EC2 instances"
}

variable "KKE_INSTANCE_TYPE" {
  type        = string
  description = "EC2 instance type"
}

variable "KKE_KEY_NAME" {
  type        = string
  description = "EC2 key pair name"
}

variable "KKE_INSTANCE_PREFIX" {
  type        = string
  description = "EC2 instance naming prefix"
}
```

These variables make the configuration reusable and allow deployment settings to be managed separately from the EC2 resource.

## 3. AMI Data Source and Local Variable

**File: `locals.tf`**

```hcl
data "aws_ami" "amazon_linux_2" {
  most_recent = true
  owners      = ["amazon"]

  filter {
    name   = "name"
    values = ["amzn2-ami-hvm-*-x86_64-gp2"]
  }

  filter {
    name   = "virtualization-type"
    values = ["hvm"]
  }
}

locals {
  AMI_ID = data.aws_ami.amazon_linux_2.id
}
```

The data source searches for the most recent matching Amazon Linux 2 AMI. The local variable `AMI_ID` makes the retrieved AMI available to the EC2 resource.

## 4. Variable Assignments

**File: `terraform.tfvars`**

```hcl
KKE_INSTANCE_COUNT  = 3
KKE_INSTANCE_TYPE   = "t2.micro"
KKE_KEY_NAME        = "devops-key"
KKE_INSTANCE_PREFIX = "devops-instance"
```

## 5. Terraform Output

**File: `outputs.tf`**

```hcl
output "kke_instance_names" {
  description = "Names of the EC2 instances created"
  value       = [for instance in aws_instance.kke_instance : instance.tags["Name"]]
}
```

This output returns the names of all three provisioned EC2 instances.

